    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Yes, hail damage is typically covered by standard homeowners insurance policies in Utah.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What is Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Dwelling Coverage: Helps repair or replace your home's physical structure, including your roof, siding, windows, and attached structures.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Other Structures: Covers detached buildings on your property, such as sheds, fences, or detached garages.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Personal Property: Can pay to repair or replace belongings inside your home (like furniture or electronics) if hail causes a roof or window breach that ruins them.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Details to Know in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wind and Hail Deductibles: Many Utah policies feature a separate wind and hail deductible rather than a standard flat-rate deductible. This is frequently calculated as a percentage of your total dwelling coverage (such as 1% or 2%) rather than a set $1,000 fee.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cosmetic vs. Functional Damage: Some policies in hail-prone regions include a cosmetic damage exclusion, meaning the insurer may deny a claim if the hail alters the appearance of your roof or siding without impairing its actual structural function.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Actual Cash Value (ACV) vs. Replacement Cost: Check whether your roof is covered at its replacement cost value (RCV) or depreciated actual cash value (ACV) based on its age.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Vehicles Are Excluded: Hail damage to your cars parked outside is not covered by your homeowners insurance; it requires comprehensive coverage on your auto insurance policy.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flooding is Excluded: If heavy rain or hail leads to ground-level flooding, standard homeowners policies will not cover it\u2014you need a separate flood insurance policy.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              10
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can check state guidelines or file questions through the Utah Insurance Department .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          11
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of damage you are seeing (roof, siding, windows, etc.)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roughly how old your roof is"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you understand what steps to take next."
      }
    ],
